WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.702
[dramatic music playing]

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.012
MALE SPEAKER: This
is it, Albert.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.147
Welcome to the jungle.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.719
We are on sacred
grounds right now.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:26.726
You're just beginning to
see part of the structures.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.929
ALBERT LIN: I've never
seen anything like this.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.363
MALE SPEAKER:
Welcome to Nan Madol.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.468
ALBERT LIN: (VOICEOVER)
Only a tiny fragment

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:40.507
of the legendary Soudelor
city can still be seen.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.309
Mangroves choke
whatever else remains.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.150
Now, new technology
can help unlock

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.319
the secrets of this place.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:59.592
How and why it was built, and
just how big it really is.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.327
What is that?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.931
It's incredible, isn't it?

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.232
I was born here.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.701
But every time I come up
here, I'm always amazed.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.370
Always.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.640
This is the main ceremonial
center of Nan Madol.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.109
[majestic music playing]

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.113
ALBERT LIN: (VOICEOVER)
It's a temple

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.850
to the island's ancient
rulers, constructed

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:27.353
from pillars of basalt rock.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.123
800 years ago, this place
would have been bustling

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.959
with hundreds of
priests, attendants,

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.360
and the feared Soudelor kings.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.935
Must have been some
super-powered humans

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.503
to build this, huh?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.539
Well, this area was
meant only for the elite.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.042
It was the only
time in our history

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.479
that we were ruled by one
person, almost like a dictator.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.080
So he was able to
command all the people

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:57.584
on the island to come and assist
in the building of Nan Modal.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.052
Look, is that more
rocks over there?

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.220
Is that even more of them?

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.921
That's an outer
wall, built all the way

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.323
to the edge of the reef.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.191
Yeah, you can see the
reef breaking, right there.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.059
Exactly.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:06.860
It's massive.

00:02:09.127 --> 00:02:10.363
ALBERT LIN: (VOICEOVER)
To get to grips

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.666
with this "city in the
sea," we need to work

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.935
out the full extent of it.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.572
And that can only
be done from above.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.042
I think we have to
scan this with the drone.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.477
And maybe we can start
to really map out

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.813
all these different features.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.816
OK, so this is where
we're at right now.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.886
There are 90-plus
structures, all man-made.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.821
From here, all the
way down south.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.589
You had your exit--
- All the way to there?

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.257
Yes.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.157
Such a huge area.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.260
It is huge.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.094
Can't see anything.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.029
It's all mangrove.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.498
Were the mangroves
here 800 years ago?

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.900
No, I doubt it.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.002
It's been abandoned for a long
time, so mangroves just grew.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.804
It would have been easier
to map it then than it is now.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.239
Well, that's why
we have LIDAR, right?

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.742
We're gonna delete
the mangroves.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.278
Taking off.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.313
[drone whirring]

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.620
ALBERT LIN: (VOICEOVER) My drone
team begin the first of more

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.558
than 40 planned flights.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:15.528
We're scanning this whole area,
almost half a square mile--

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.564
twice the size of
the Vatican City.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.802
We want to strip back
the jungle canopy

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.738
and reveal the rest of the city.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.608
[dramatic music playing]

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.480
I'm going back to explore the
gigantic building that Gus

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.650
showed me to find out
more about the people who

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.685
built this place.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.191
Why is there so little
known about the people that

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.628
built this incredible monument?

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.530
The reason there
is so little known

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:55.201
is because there's not a
written system to express ideas.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.737
It's through oral
tradition, which are--

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.571
Stories.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.906
Exactly.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.674
Those are stories handed down,
generation to generation.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:05.111
And no person can tell the
entire story because there's

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.779
the belief that, if they
tell the whole story,

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.714
that they will die.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.414
They're no longer useful.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.886
ALBERT LIN: How was
this place built?

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.022
I can't imagine how human
effort could actually

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:19.459
carry these stones all the way
up to the top of this building.

00:04:19.524 --> 00:04:21.661
It's really not clear
to us how it was done--

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.830
the physics part of it.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.333
One legend talks about magic
being used to lift the rocks

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.700
and bring them over here.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.268
So they would fly.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.538
Magic flew these rocks here.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.707
That's right.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.275
ALBERT LIN: (VOICEOVER)
This whole expedition

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.244
is something else.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.580
I'm a scientist, a technologist.

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.448
I deal in facts.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:45.551
Finding out how they
actually built this?

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.887
It's going to be a challenge.

